+++ b/specs/002-task-timestamps/spec.md
@@ -0,0 +1,9 @@
+# Feature Specification: Task timestamps
+
+- **FR-001**: Every task has `createdAt` and `updatedAt`, ISO-8601 date-time strings; equal when added.
+- **FR-002**: complete, reopen, rename, tag and untag set `updatedAt` to the time of the change; `createdAt` never changes.
+- **FR-003**: The domain does not read the clock (constitution): `createTaskList(now)` takes a time source; `createTodoList(now?)` defaults to the real clock outside the domain.
+- **FR-004**: A failed operation changes nothing.
+
+## Assumptions
+- Tagging a task with a tag it has, or untagging one it lacks, still counts as a change attempt and sets `updatedAt`.
